{"step_index":28,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-05T21:47:12Z","input_tokens":3029,"cache_read_tokens":40350,"output_tokens":1678,"thinking":"Network adapter information reveals the default gateway's MAC address matches a MikroTik RouterBOARD. This suggests the network utilizes a MikroTik router. Investigating the MikroTik router's configuration becomes the next logical step.\n\n\nChecking if the MikroTik router exposes common management interfaces: HTTP, SSH, Winbox, SNMP. This information is needed to understand the current configuration. Given the user's explicit request to examine the MikroTik, and that it is on their network, I can proceed with this check.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"# 1. Port check on 192.168.10.1\n$ports = @(21, 22, 23, 53, 80, 443, 2000, 8080, 8291, 8728, 8729)\nforeach ($p in $ports) {\n    $tcp = New-Object System.Net.Sockets.TcpClient\n    $connect = $tcp.BeginConnect(\"192.168.10.1\", $p, $null, $null)\n    $wait = $connect.AsyncWaitHandle.WaitOne(400, $false)\n    if ($wait -and $tcp.Connected) {\n        Write-Host \"Port $p : OPEN\"\n    } else {\n        Write-Host \"Port $p : CLOSED\"\n    }\n    $tcp.Close()\n}\n\n# 2. HTTP WebFig check\ntry {\n    $resp = Invoke-WebRequest -Uri \"http://192.168.10.1\" -UseBasicParsing -TimeoutSec 3\n    Write-Host \"HTTP Status: $($resp.StatusCode)\"\n    $resp.Content.Substring(0, [Math]::Min(1000, $resp.Content.Length))\n} catch {\n    Write-Host \"HTTP error: $_\"\n}\n\n# 3. MNDP Discovery (UDP 5678)\ntry {\n    $udp = New-Object System.Net.Sockets.UdpClient(5678)\n    $udp.Client.ReceiveTimeout = 3000\n    $ep = New-Object System.Net.IPEndPoint([System.Net.IPAddress]::Broadcast, 5678)\n    $bytes = [byte[]](0,0,0,0)\n    $udp.Send($bytes, $bytes.Length, \"255.255.255.255\", 5678) | Out-Null\n    $udp.Send($bytes, $bytes.Length, \"192.168.10.255\", 5678) | Out-Null\n    $udp.Send($bytes, $bytes.Length, \"192.168.10.1\", 5678) | Out-Null\n    $start = Get-Date\n    while (((Get-Date) - $start).TotalSeconds -lt 4) {\n        $remoteEp = New-Object System.Net.IPEndPoint([System.Net.IPAddress]::Any, 0)\n        $data = $udp.Receive([ref]$remoteEp)\n        if ($data.Length -gt 4) {\n            Write-Host \"MNDP Packet from $($remoteEp.Address) ($($data.Length) bytes):\"\n            $pos = 4\n            while ($pos + 4 -le $data.Length) {\n                $type = [BitConverter]::ToUInt16($data, $pos)\n                if ([BitConverter]::IsLittleEndian) {\n                    $type = [uint16](($data[$pos] -shl 8) -bor $data[$pos+1])\n                    $len = [uint16](($data[$pos+2] -shl 8) -bor $data[$pos+3])\n                }\n                $pos += 4\n                if ($pos + $len -le $data.Length) {\n                    $valBytes = $data[$pos..($pos+$len-1)]\n                    $strVal = [System.Text.Encoding]::ASCII.GetString($valBytes)\n                    $hexVal = ($valBytes | ForEach-Object { $_.ToString(\"X2\") }) -join \":\"\n                    Write-Host \"  TLV Type $type (len $len): ASCII='$strVal' HEX=$hexVal\"\n                }\n                $pos += $len\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    $udp.Close()\n} catch {\n    Write-Host \"MNDP finished/timeout: $_\"\n    if ($udp) { $udp.Close() }\n}","WaitMsBeforeAsync":10000,"toolSummary":"Inspect MikroTik at 192.168.10.1 via ports, HTTP, and MNDP"}}]}
