{"step_index":32,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-05T21:47:50Z","input_tokens":3721,"cache_read_tokens":45666,"output_tokens":1105,"thinking":"MNDP discovery shows the system receiving its own broadcast, then the MikroTik's response immediately after. Suspect the process needs to skip the first broadcast packet to correctly interpret the MikroTik's response. The next step is to create a loop that ignores the initial self-broadcast.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"# 1. MNDP Discovery (read multiple packets so we get the router's reply)\ntry {\n    $localEp = New-Object System.Net.IPEndPoint([System.Net.IPAddress]::Parse(\"192.168.10.228\"), 5678)\n    $udp = New-Object System.Net.Sockets.UdpClient($localEp)\n    $udp.EnableBroadcast = $true\n    $udp.Client.ReceiveTimeout = 3000\n    $bytes = [byte[]](0,0,0,0)\n    $udp.Send($bytes, $bytes.Length, \"255.255.255.255\", 5678) | Out-Null\n    for ($i = 0; $i -lt 5; $i++) {\n        $remoteEp = New-Object System.Net.IPEndPoint([System.Net.IPAddress]::Any, 0)\n        $data = $udp.Receive([ref]$remoteEp)\n        if ($data.Length -gt 4) {\n            Write-Host \"Received MNDP from $($remoteEp.Address) ($($data.Length) bytes)\"\n            $pos = 4\n            while ($pos + 4 -le $data.Length) {\n                $type = [uint16](($data[$pos] -shl 8) -bor $data[$pos+1])\n                $len = [uint16](($data[$pos+2] -shl 8) -bor $data[$pos+3])\n                $pos += 4\n                if ($pos + $len -le $data.Length -and $len -gt 0) {\n                    $valBytes = $data[$pos..($pos+$len-1)]\n                    $strVal = [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8.GetString($valBytes)\n                    $hexVal = ($valBytes | ForEach-Object { $_.ToString(\"X2\") }) -join \":\"\n                    Write-Host (\"  TLV {0,2} (len {1,2}): ASCII='{2}' | HEX={3}\" -f $type, $len, $strVal, $hexVal)\n                }\n                $pos += $len\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    $udp.Close()\n} catch {\n    if ($udp) { $udp.Close() }\n}\n\n# 2. Test RouterOS API (8728) with default admin / empty password\ntry {\n    $tcp = New-Object System.Net.Sockets.TcpClient(\"192.168.10.1\", 8728)\n    $stream = $tcp.GetStream()\n    $stream.ReadTimeout = 2000\n    function Send-RosWord($s, [string]$w) {\n        $b = [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8.GetBytes($w)\n        $s.WriteByte([byte]$b.Length)\n        $s.Write($b, 0, $b.Length)\n    }\n    Send-RosWord $stream \"/login\"\n    Send-RosWord $stream \"=name=admin\"\n    Send-RosWord $stream \"=password=\"\n    $stream.WriteByte(0)\n    $buf = New-Object byte[] 512\n    $read = $stream.Read($buf, 0, 512)\n    $reply = [System.Text.Encoding]::ASCII.GetString($buf, 0, $read)\n    Write-Host \"API Login Reply ($read bytes): $reply\"\n    $tcp.Close()\n} catch {\n    Write-Host \"API test error: $_\"\n}","WaitMsBeforeAsync":8000,"toolSummary":"Read MNDP device details and test default API login on 192.168.10.1"}}]}
