{"step_index":53,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-05T22:31:30Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nok conecte un microtik quiero que el puerto 1 me de internet de cualquier ip sin restricciones \n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-11-05T16:31:30-06:00.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
{"step_index":54,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-05T22:31:30Z","input_tokens":65466,"cache_read_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1655,"thinking":"Initial assumption is the user wants to configure a MikroTik router's port to provide unrestricted internet access. Need to verify the current network state to understand the existing configuration before applying any changes.\n\n\nThe previous attempt to connect directly to the router's login port was blocked. Avoid direct connections for now. Prepare RouterOS commands and a `.rsc` script. The goal is to interpret the user's intent: to grant unrestricted internet access to a port, potentially in two scenarios.\n\nFirst, consider the case where the port (`ether1`) receives internet from a modem/router via DHCP.\n\n\nTwo distinct scenarios for unrestricted internet access are identified: Scenario A involves NAT without firewall restrictions across all ports; Scenario B centers on using `ether1` either directly or as part of a bridge with Universal NAT functionality, enabling devices with static or dynamic IPs to connect without restrictions. The setup will generate a ready-to-use `.rsc` script.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"# ==============================================================================\n# PLANTILLA 05: PUERTO 1 (ether1) CON INTERNET DE CUALQUIER IP SIN RESTRICCIONES\n# Compatible con MikroTik RouterOS v6 y v7\n# ==============================================================================\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# OPCIÓN A: EL CABLE DEL MÓDEM ENTRA EN EL PUERTO 1 (ether1) Y ACEPTA CUALQUIER\n# IP AUTOMÁTICAMENTE, DANDO INTERNET LIBRE Y SIN RESTRICCIONES A TODOS LOS PUERTOS\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n# 1. Asegurar que ether1 esté libre (fuera de cualquier bridge) para recibir Internet de cualquier IP\n/interface bridge port remove [find interface=ether1]\n\n# 2. Activar Cliente DHCP en ether1 para aceptar automáticamente cualquier IP, Gateway y DNS del proveedor\n/ip dhcp-client remove [find interface=ether1]\n/ip dhcp-client add interface=ether1 disabled=no add-default-route=yes default-route-distance=1 use-peer-dns=yes use-peer-ntp=yes comment=\"WAN Puerto 1 - Recibir Internet de cualquier IP\"\n\n# 3. Activar DNS para responder a cualquier solicitud\n/ip dns set servers=1.1.1.1,8.8.8.8,1.0.0.1,8.8.4.4 allow-remote-requests=yes\n\n# 4. Limpiar restricciones de Firewall (Input, Forward, RAW) para permitir tráfico total sin bloqueos\n/ip firewall raw remove [find]\n/ip firewall filter remove [find]\n/ip firewall filter add chain=input action=accept comment=\"Permitir todo hacia el router sin restricciones\"\n/ip firewall filter add chain=forward action=accept comment=\"Permitir todo el trafico de Internet desde cualquier IP sin restricciones\"\n\n# 5. NAT Universal (Masquerade) para que CUALQUIER IP origen salga a Internet por ether1\n/ip firewall nat remove [find]\n/ip firewall nat add chain=srcnat out-interface=ether1 action=masquerade comment=\"NAT Universal por Puerto 1 para cualquier IP\"\n/ip firewall nat add chain=srcnat action=masquerade comment=\"Respaldo NAT global para cualquier interfaz/IP\"\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# OPCIÓN B: SI CONECTAS TU PC/EQUIPOS EN EL PUERTO 1 (ether1) Y QUIERES QUE EL\n# PUERTO 1 ENTREGUE INTERNET (MODO SWITCH / PUENTE EN TODOS LOS PUERTOS)\n# (Ejecuta este bloque si el Internet entra por otro puerto o Wi-Fi y quieres\n#  que ether1 dé Internet a lo que conectes en él)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# /ip dhcp-client remove [find interface=ether1]\n# /interface bridge port add bridge=[/interface bridge find name~\"bridge|lan|LAN\" ] interface=ether1\n# /ip firewall filter remove [find]\n# /ip firewall nat add chain=srcnat action=masquerade comment=\"NAT para cualquier IP\"\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"C:\\Users\\andre\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\microtik\\microtik\\00_Plantillas_RSC_Listas_Para_Usar\\05_puerto1_internet_sin_restricciones.rsc"}}]}
